course: dictionary
lesson: 10173
title: Tide: the sea and beyond
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Check the tide times before you walk on the shore.» Tide times are about the sea, so tide here means the sea rising and falling.
explain: The sea rises and falls twice a day, mainly because of the pull of the Moon's gravity. At high tide the beach gets smaller, and at low tide you can explore rock pools. «The tide comes in across flat sand faster than you can walk» shows why the tide matters for safety.
explain: Tide also means a strong feeling or trend that changes, as in a tide of opinion. As a verb, «tide someone over» means help them for a short time until something better comes, like «a snack to tide you over until dinner». To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A tide is the regular rise and fall of the sea's level, usually twice a day.
fact: Tides are caused mainly by the pull of the Moon's gravity, and the Sun's gravity pulls too.
fact: High tide and low tide come roughly every 12 and a half hours.
fact: «Tide» can also mean a strong feeling or trend that changes, as in a tide of opinion.
fact: «Tide someone over» means help them for a short time until something better comes.
exercise: «The tide comes in across flat sand faster than you can walk.» What is the tide in this sentence? | A strong feeling that changes | A kind of sand | A type of boat | *The sea rising and falling
exercise: «A snack to tide you over until dinner.» What does tide over mean? | To fall asleep early | To wash someone away into the sea | To rise and fall twice a day | *To help someone for a short time until something better comes
exercise: «Lifeguards move the flags during the day, because the safe place changes as the tide and currents change.» Why do the flags move? | *Because the sea rises and falls, so the safe place changes | Because the Moon is full | Because the sand is hot | Because the flags are heavy and blow away
test: «Mangroves grow with their feet in the sea water where the tide comes in and out twice a day.» How often does the tide come in and out here? | Every hour | Once a week | *Twice a day | Once a year
test: In «a tide of opinion», what does tide mean? | To help someone for a short time | *A strong feeling or trend that changes | A small wave on the beach | The regular rise and fall of the sea
exam: Which is the best meaning of tide in «Check the tide times before you walk on the shore, because an incoming tide can cut you off on a sandbank»? | A kind of fish | *The regular rise and fall of the sea's level | A strong feeling that changes | To help someone for a short time
